course: dictionary
lesson: 9036
title: A slat is a thin strip
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A slat is a long, thin, flat strip of wood, metal or plastic. Slats usually come in a row with gaps between them, like the bars on a bed or a park bench.
explain: Read the words around the word to find its meaning. «The sunlight came through the slats of the blind» tells you slats are the thin strips you can tilt to let light in. Ask: what would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
explain: Look for the gaps. Slats are one of a row, with spaces between them, so the word means a single strip in a line, not a big solid piece of wood.
fact: A slat is a long, thin, flat strip.
fact: Slats are usually one of a row, with gaps between them.
fact: «Wooden slats» are strips of wood.
fact: «Bed slats» are the strips that hold up the mattress.
fact: «Between the slats» means through the gaps.
fact: A pencil is made with graphite sandwiched between «two slats of cedar wood».
fact: Aeroplane wings have «flaps and slats» that help the plane fly slowly without falling.
exercise: «The bench had wooden slats.» What is a slat? | A round ball of wool | A large window of glass | *A long, thin, flat strip of wood | A small, soft cushion
exercise: «The sunlight came through the slats of the blind.» Where are the slats? | Under the bath | Inside a bag of sweets | *On a blind, in a row with gaps | In the sky
exercise: The pencil has «two slats of cedar wood». What shape are slats? | Square like a box | *Long, thin and flat | Round like a ball | Soft and fluffy
test: A row of slats usually has what between them? | *Gaps | Water | Paint | Stones
test: «Flaps and slats slide out of the wing» at take-off. What does this help the plane do? | Sink into the sea | Go faster than sound | Turn into a boat | *Fly slowly without falling
exam: Which word means nearly the same as slat? | Lamp | Button | *Strip | Cloud
